WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
<v Omar Haddad>Morning all. Ana, where are we with the migration?</v>

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Ana Souza>Honestly the old claim codes are what's holding us up. About a third of them don't map cleanly to the new categories.</v>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Ana Souza>I can get a first pass of the mapping table across to Omar by Thursday.</v>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Omar Haddad>That'd be great. Ben, could you ask Grace's team for the list of retired codes?</v>

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.000
<v Ben Wu>Sure, I'll ping them this afternoon.</v>

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Omar Haddad>On the keys: I'd say we keep the legacy claim numbers as the primary key and add the new ID alongside.</v>

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Grace Kim>Yeah, let's go with that. Adjusters search by the old number anyway.</v>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Ana Souza>Do we actually need to bring across closed claims older than seven years?</v>

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:14.000
<v Grace Kim>Honestly not sure, that's a legal call. Leave it with me, I'll find out from legal.</v>

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.000
<v Ana Souza>If the mapping isn't done by the end of the month we'll start eating into the code freeze.</v>

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.000
<v Omar Haddad>Understood. Let's keep an eye on it.</v>
